11.0.0 — answers to the sixteen-bar recording: modulation you can see, a tempo you can hold, breaks in time, finer values

New since 10083, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Modulation: every route is a row under its track in Arrange — its depth as a value in tenths of
  a percent, On, From Zero / Centred, Remove. A value that a route or an automation lane moves
  wears an "M" or "A", and VoiceOver says so. Modulate checks a pair already routed instead of
  adding it twice.
- Tempo: while Flow moves the tempo, the number reads "FLOW · Tap to Hold"; one tap keeps the
  tempo it reached.
- Breaks: Slice to Pads cuts a busy loop on its grid, one pad per step, each on its own hit, so the
  pattern plays in time and keeps the feel at any song tempo.
- Values read as fine as they are set: hertz to hundredths below 100 Hz, milliseconds to a tenth,
  and a time or slow rate names its note value at the song's tempo ("375 ms 1/8 dotted").
- Arrange: track rows grow into the free room (up to twice as high); names may take two lines; a
  new track never repeats another's name.
- Note editor: Undo and Redo in its own bar. Automation lanes show a point's value while it is
  dragged. The step grid marks beats at any step size and meter.
- Add Track › Drums opens the new beat's steps at once.
- VoiceOver: moving, trimming and fading in Arrange say where things landed or why not; fine value
  fields swipe in useful steps; a plugin's automation lane is named by its parameter.
Limits, new: notes are still chosen one at a time in the note editor; a sample click above 300 BPM
is cut by the next one.
Older limits as in 10083.

Previous: 10083. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10083. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen bars in two
to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol; stop wherever
it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the way in it is
the next work, in the order it happened.

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
